  "notes": {
    "overlay-check": "Decides what happens with each entry an interpretation writes.",
    "overlay-check.calcs.entry": "An entry of the interpretation, given what is already under its name: nothing, prose Layer 1 wrote, code Layer 1 wrote, or an entry of the interpretation itself; whether that is under the same heading; whether the heading is closed to new entries (Layer 1 wrote the commands or queries heading); and whether only Layer 1 may write the heading (examples, components). When something is there: under another heading it is wrong-heading; the interpretation's own entry written again is twice; Layer 1's code cannot be overwritten (overwrite); Layer 1's prose is filled. When nothing is there: a closed heading refuses it (closed-heading), a heading only Layer 1 writes refuses it (layer1-only), and otherwise it is added."
